  "insights": {
    "creative": "The night class video, which opens 'Some skills can be automated. Cooking professionally isn't one of them,' brought 15 Meta form leads at $11.52. The two 'A real skill is earned, not handed out' videos brought 8 each, at $10.77 and $8.84. The tour ad, 'Nothing about this program has to be taken on faith. Book a tour and see it for yourself,' brought 4 at $9.37. Worth testing a kitchen walk-through video on that tour invitation, since it brought low-cost leads on little spend.",
    "doing": "All form fills were 31 at $25.79 each, up from 24 at $31.38 the week before; that count includes organic and Google fills. Meta brought 16 leads at $35.95, against 13 at $41.92, and 7 campus tours were booked.",
    "look_into": "Google brought 3 leads at $74.75 each, against $35.95 on Meta and up from $69.39 the week before. Meta also counted 39 form leads on its side while 16 reached the CRM with a Facebook link, so that gap is still worth checking.",
    "next": "We recommend testing a move of part of the night class budget to the main campaign for a week, since the main campaign brought 20 Meta form leads at $10.86 each against 19 at $18.85 for night class."
